    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d725">

                <pb facs="0740" n="728" xml:id="pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10379: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-05-03T15:00:00-04:00">May 3, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Your No. 111, April 26, 4 p.m., last sentence. The Department does not
                    consider it desirable to comply with Hugessen’s suggestion since he is in
                    communication with his Government and it would be inappropriate for the
                    Department to initiate discussions involving primarily Anglo-Turkish
                    relations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
